 "notes": "Generated-row sibling (#4507) of genapp-lgupdb01: CUSTOMER, POLICY and the ENDOWMENT / HOUSE / MOTOR / COMMERCIAL tables are generated from base/cntl/db2cre.jcl (the same generate block as genapp-lgipdb01-generated: identity policy numbers 1000001..1000012 (the requests carry them), FKs POLICY->CUSTOMER and type->POLICY, NULLs and boundary values), not GenApp's INSERTs. The scenarios are written against those seed 4507 rows: each names a customer, a policy and the row's LASTCHANGED (the optimistic lock) as the generated POLICY row holds it; LGUPVS01's KSDSPOLY (ksdspoly.txt) holds a record for each policy that reaches it. Covered: the three types on generated policies, the lowest and highest timestamps, a NULL BROKERID and a NULL BROKERSREFERENCE read through their indicators, a stale LASTCHANGED ('02'), a request for a type the policy does not hold (+100 '01'), a wrong customer and an unknown policy (FETCH +100). Not generated: policies 4 and 5, whose ISSUEDATE / EXPIRYDATE are NULL (the FETCH has no indicator for them: -305, '90', WRITE-ERROR-MESSAGE LINKs LGSTSQ, oracle_assumptions.md X6), and the paths on which LGUPVS01 fails. A change to the generator's draw moves the rows: the E2E test in tests/cobol_mainframe/test_equivalence_db2_rows.py fails the case then. Program, LINKed LGUPVS01 and the LGCMAREA COMMAREA as in genapp-lgupdb01.",
